{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3647","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3647","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3647\",\"parent_revision\":\"408ef99ae69816e951b5824b9e536d1463b3a114\",\"root_revision\":\"2c1227dc32ff2fadc5da004353cc84265d0694dfe90433ae4898aa9c9f144a7b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe groom workflow requires each acceptance criterion to be an observable check, with no architecture decisions or proposed solutions (`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md:267`). #3060 finished grooming with two criteria that break that rule:\\n\\n- AC 2 names mechanisms (`navigate=`, `map=True`) and leaves the choice between them open: \\\"determined by the architect phase's resolution ... either (a) ... (b) ... or (c)\\\".\\n- AC 4 lists test function names that must keep passing.\\n\\nThe architecture spec later chose option (b). AC 2 was never rewritten to state that choice.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen a criterion checks which solution was chosen, not whether the outcome holds, a false premise passes every gate that reads the criteria.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nWhen planning or implementation starts, every acceptance criterion on a groomed item is a fixed, observable check.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: no step between the architect phase and implementation writes a design decision back into the item's acceptance criteria.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nWhen planning or implementation starts, every acceptance criterion on a groomed item is a fixed, observable check.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: no step between the architect phase and implementation writes a design decision back into the item's acceptance criteria.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-09-19: the repo owner's review of #3060's acceptance criteria\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #3060 carries `status:groomed` with AC 2 and AC 4 in this form.\\n- Option (b) was accepted because `map=True` \\\"is documented as always under 2,000 tokens\\\". #3059 shows that MAP has no size limit.\\n- An observable outcome would be: \\\"an agent that narrowed to one over-budget section, and follows the hint, gets that section's content without any response going over the budget\\\". Option (b) fails that check on large items. AC 2, as written, accepts it.\\n- PR #3642 implements (b). Its tests pass against AC 2 as written.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b4eb9375bc7cc65e1f22be6909d8f4a74816d6a053ce5f5542345dea19df5089\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVoII4Q\"}"}